  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "MI4mLYQ83BEWImbphXct+uyORjI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:43:49.582Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`packages/shared` is an npm package for code shared across the monorepo, and it carries one rule in bold: it **\"should never depend on any other package in this monorepo.\"** The reason is stated directly \u2014 so the code kept there can be used in *any* other package without circular imports.\n\nWhat belongs there follows from the rule:\n\n- simple constants usable anywhere;\n- **base** types worth sharing easily \u2014 explicitly **not** derived types that require imports from elsewhere;\n- simple utility functions that do not depend on code from elsewhere in the monorepo.\n\nThis constraint is visible in the reactor's own layering. `IProcessorHostModuleBase` lives in shared and carries only host-agnostic fields; `client` is added by `@powerhousedao/reactor` and `attachments` by reactor-browser and reactor-api, \"since neither shared nor reactor can depend on reactor-attachments\". The layering is not stylistic \u2014 it is this rule applied.\n\nSo when a type feels like it belongs in shared but needs an import, the answer is a base type in shared plus an extension in the package that owns the dependency.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/shared/README.md` \u2014 whole file (the never-depend rule and what belongs there)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:43:49.582Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:43:49.582Z"
    }
  },
  {
